# ==============================================================================
# vorbis-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# LINE 1 IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores names that also occur inside the vendored Xiph source trees and in
# this tooling, for example:
#
#     [Ww][Ii][Nn]32/    -> ogg/win32/ and vorbis/win32/ (part of the upstream
#                           release tarballs)
#     *.env              -> linux/pins.env
#     [Dd]ebug/  [Rr]elease/  [Oo]ut/  [Ll]og/ ...
#
# Without the "!*" below, such files would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the vendored snapshots would no longer match their tarballs in
# upstream-downloads/. A nested .gitignore takes precedence over the ones above
# it, so re-including everything here and then re-ignoring only what this
# folder genuinely produces is the correct fix - and it keeps the root
# .gitignore untouched. (Same arrangement as CodeBrix.Sdl3's sdl3-native-tools.)
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git check-ignore -v vorbis-native-tools/vorbis/win32/vorbis.def
#     git check-ignore -v vorbis-native-tools/linux/pins.env
#         -> should print nothing (i.e. the file is NOT ignored)
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built native libraries, unstripped copies, smoke-test binaries, BUILD-INFO,
# the host build for the managed tests. ONE tree, shared by every platform
# build, so all RIDs land side by side.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH MATTERS: without it the pattern would match ANY directory
# named "output" at any depth. The trailing /* (not a bare /output/) leaves the
# directory visible so the README negation below can work.
/output/*
!/output/README.txt

# Local scratch that the scripts may leave behind.
*.tmp
*.log
build-scratch/

# Finder droppings (the "!*" above overrides any inherited .DS_Store rule).
.DS_Store
